# C2-S10, the Clock Tower, B02 The Minute Hand, C2-S11 The Missing Shift.
# Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 2345–2407.
# "bell" plays in the region when the player approaches the tower; the rest in
# scenes/chapter2/clock_tower.tscn.

# C2-S10 — the bell rings thirteen times, then stops.
~ bell
do bell_thirteen
Kaelen (Internal): ...eleven. Twelve. Thirteen.
# Then silence. Merchants stop. Children count on their fingers. Paladins look up.
Brask: Seal the lower streets.
Seraphina: We don't know what's happened yet.
Brask: That is why we seal them.
do data_vision_trace
System: TRACE: CLOCK AUTHORITY CONFLICT.
System: TRACE: LEGACY SCHEDULES ACTIVE.
System: TRACE: EXTERNAL ADMIN PROXY.
Kaelen: Something's running that tower that isn't the tower.
Seraphina: Then we go up and ask it.
[if ch2_medicine_quest_active and not ch2_medicine_done] Seraphina: And the convoy's still out. That was the evening bell, Kaelen. The west gate's closing.
set ch2_tower_bell_stopped

~ entry
Kaelen: The gears on this floor are all running at different times.
Elara: They're arguing.
Kaelen: That's... actually exactly what they're doing.
Kaelen (Internal): I can slow one down with Root Access. Not stop it. Safely, a little.

# A mark scratched into the wall on the way up (a seed for Kaito, later).
~ mid
Kaelen (Internal): Somebody's scratched a little map mark into the stone. Under it: NO SKY ABOVE FLOOR SIX.
Elara: Is there sky above floor six?
Kaelen: I'm not going to check.
set ch2_tower_secret_mark

~ pre_boss
System: SCHEDULE DEVIATION.
Kaelen: That's us. We're the deviation.
Seraphina: I've hated clocks before.
Seraphina: This is new.

# ── B02 The Minute Hand: barks, one line each ─────────────────────────────
~ bark_deviation
The Minute Hand: SCHEDULE DEVIATION.

~ bark_correct
The Minute Hand: CORRECT.

~ bark_replay
The Minute Hand: REPLAYING.

~ victory
Kaelen: Half the tower's ours again. Half.
System: SHIFT LOG: LOWER WORKS, SHIFT FOUR — ENTERED 06:00. EXIT: NONE.
set ch2_clock_tower_complete
=> missing_shift

# C2-S11 — the missing shift. Not the faction choice; every option costs something.
~ missing_shift
Seraphina: Forty workers went into the tunnels this morning. None of them came out.
Brask: Then we quarantine the tunnels until we know what's down there.
Seraphina: We know what's down there. Forty people.
? Kaelen (Internal): It's not my city. They're asking me anyway.
- We go now. Every hour matters. => rescue_now
- We scout first, and know what we're walking into. => scout_first
- Seal it until morning. Nobody else goes missing tonight. => seal

~ rescue_now
set ch2_shift_rescue_now
do trust seraphina 10
Seraphina: Good. Get your things.
Brask: If you lose a single paladin down there, Commander—
Seraphina: Then you'll write it down, and I'll read it.
=> unlock

~ scout_first
set ch2_shift_scout_first
Seraphina: That'll cost us hours.
Kaelen: It'll cost more if we walk in blind.
Seraphina: ...Fine. Hours. Not one minute more.
=> unlock

~ seal
set ch2_shift_sealed
do trust seraphina -10
Brask: Thank you.
Seraphina: Don't thank him. He just bought whatever's down there a whole night to get worse.
=> unlock

~ unlock
set ch2_underground_unlocked
